  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C59"],
      "pins": ["C59.1", "C59.2"],
      "nets": ["+24V", "GND"],
      "observed": "C59 is connected from the +24 V rail to GND, but its schematic value is 220n and the SPICE deck also models it as 220 nF. Its footprint, part number, and description fields identify it as a 220 µF 50 V Kemet electrolytic capacitor.",
      "expected": "The specification states C59 should be 220 µF, consistent with the bulk 24 V decoupling capacitors C2/C58/C60.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C59\")\n      (value \"220n\")\n      (footprint \"Coert-Vonk:CAP ALUM 220μF ±20 50V Kemet\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"3\") (name \"+24V\") ... (node (ref \"C59\") (pin \"1\") ... ) ... (net (code \"76\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"C59\") (pin \"2\") ... )"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "C59 +24V 0 220n"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2/C58/C59/C60 220µF distributed near loads"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the 220 nF value is the actual populated part or the value used for sourcing/simulation, the 24 V bulk rail loses one intended 220 µF decoupling capacitor, reducing low-frequency energy storage and potentially increasing rail noise or transient instability near the buck regulator and motor drivers.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The connectivity and component roles largely match the specification, but C59 shows a clear value mismatch: it is modeled and valued as 220 nF while the specification and its own part metadata identify it as a 220 µF bulk capacitor on the +24 V rail."
}

